    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/gado_gado?rev=1625791090&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-07-08T20:38:10-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:gado_gado - created</title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/gado_gado?rev=1625791090&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Gado-Gado

By Hetty McKinnon (in NYT) 7-8-21
YIELD6 to 8 servings
TIME45 minutes

Gado-gado is a beloved dish across Indonesia. Each region has a different spin: In Jakarta, it is a “double-carb” dish, featuring both potato and lontong (rice cakes). In West Java, it is known as lotek atah or karedok and served with raw vegetables. At the heart of any gado-gado is the spicy peanut sauce: Some versions call for tamarind, lime, terasi (shrimp paste) or coconut milk. Others use peanut butter instead…</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/garden/garden?rev=1623610472&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-06-13T14:54:32-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:garden - [GARDEN 2018] </title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/garden/garden?rev=1623610472&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Garden 2007

Raised Beds 2007:
Bed 1, near garage, near house:
Tomatoes Brandywine, (Seeds of Change). Grew well, many tomatoes initially, then with drought, had problems with decreased production and blossom end rot. Note:  leave more room for plants and stake them well.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/garden/plantings?rev=1620953926&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-13T20:58:46-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:plantings - [2019] </title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/garden/plantings?rev=1620953926&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Garden: Plantings 2008

2007 or 2008: Corylus avellana 'contorted', “Harry lauder's Walking stick”, by garage, next to walkway to garden.
2007 or 2008, planted 2 Honeysuckle,“halls”, on either side of back porch stairs. (Direct Gardening). By 2009, they are covering the trellises there and are cold hardy. Many perfumed flowers in Spring.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/new-style_old-fashioned_chocolate_pudding?rev=1620835947&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-12T12:12:27-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:new-style_old-fashioned_chocolate_pudding - created</title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/new-style_old-fashioned_chocolate_pudding?rev=1620835947&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>New-Style Old-Fashioned Chocolate Pudding
Bon Appetit, April 1997

Ingredients 

	*  1/2 cup sugar
	*  1/3 cup unsweetened cocoa powder
	*  2 tablespoons (packed) cornstarch
	*  1 teaspoon all purpose flour
	*  Pinch of salt
	*  2 cups low-fat (1%) milk OR: 11/2 cups evaporated milk + 1/2 cup half and half or water or milk</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/garden/orchard?rev=1620515809&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-08T19:16:49-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:orchard - [2021] </title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/garden/orchard?rev=1620515809&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Garden: Orchard

04-07  planted Dwarf Patio Peach in contained round bed by garage, surrounded by mints.
( Peach: dwarf ornamental form with double pink flowers; fruit is red/gold with small white-fleshed freestone. Leaves are long slender brilliant reddish purple throughout the season. Deciduous. Useful as accent or container plant. Hardiness zone 5-9. grown by Holland Nursery, Franklin, VA 23851.  Bought at Harris teeter, Chapel Hill, $29.99.)</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/vegan_bulgogi?rev=1620489381&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-08T11:56:21-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:vegan_bulgogi - created</title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/vegan_bulgogi?rev=1620489381&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Vegan Bulgogi
(The Guardian 5-8-21)

Ingredients

	*  280g extra-ﬁrm tofu
	*  4 tbsp light soy sauce
	*  1½ tbsp brown rice syrup
	*  5 garlic cloves, peeled and crushed
	*  3cm piece fresh ginger, peeled and grated
	*  1 pear, coarsely grated
	*</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/classic_blueberry_pie?rev=1620489118&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-08T11:51:58-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf (mcf@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:classic_blueberry_pie - created</title>
        <link>https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/classic_blueberry_pie?rev=1620489118&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Classic Blueberry Pie 
(Betty Crocker.com)

Ingredients

Pastry

	*  2 cups all-purpose flour
	*  1 teaspoon salt
	*  2/3 cup shortening (cold butter or margarine)
	*  4 to 6 tablespoons cold water

Filling

	*  3/4 cup sugar
	*  1/2 cup Gold Medal™ all-purpose flour</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://hybridsky.org/w/recipes/chocolate_peanut_butter_cake?rev=1620488428&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
